+// b2384 CMV N1c (Shared Mem spec_cmv_1113, N1a's one adaptation; Planner's go): runtime data flag CMV_TAB[1], read first; 0 = v887. Bit 2: a body
+// keeps publishing its GROUP claim (engaged bit set, as RC C1188) instead of the fight-stance code ONLY when (a) its claim was ENGAGED on that group
+// last turn, (b) it is still within 3 tiles of a tile of the group, and (c) the stance code would have replaced the claim for at most 2
+// consecutive rounds so far; after that the blackout applies as live. Retreat (stance 2) and coming codes are untouched. Bit 1 (N1a) closed.
+#define CMV_BITS 0
+inline const volatile int CMV_TAB[2] = { 0x434D5632, CMV_BITS };
+#define CMV_ON(b) ((CMV_TAB[1] & (b)) != 0)
